{"name":"Orion","hex":"#de55a9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Orion","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A giant-hunter, pursuer of the Pleiades and lover of Eos, and killed by Artemis.","A constellation on the celestial equator close to Gemini and Taurus, containing the stars Betelgeuse and Rigel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Orion"}],"entries":[{"title":"Orion (constellation)","blocks":[{"text":"Orion is a prominent set of stars visible during winter in the northern celestial hemisphere. It is one of the 88 modern constellations; it was among the 48 constellations listed by the 2nd-century AD astronomer Ptolemy. It is named after a hunter in Greek mythology."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Orion_IAU.svg/330px-Orion_IAU.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orion_(constellation)","wikidata":"Q8860"},{"title":"Orion (mythology)","blocks":[{"text":"In Greek mythology, Orion was a giant huntsman whom Zeus or Artemis placed among the stars as a constellation. He was venerated as a hero in the region of Boeotia, and there is one etiological passage which says that Orion was responsible for the present shape of the Strait of Sicily."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Mosaic_House_of_Orion_by_Dr_Sophie_Hay_4.jpg/330px-Mosaic_House_of_Orion_by_Dr_Sophie_Hay_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orion_(mythology)","wikidata":"Q201261"},{"title":"Orion (spacecraft)","blocks":[{"text":"The Orion Multi-Purpose Crew Vehicle (MPCV) is a partially reusable crewed spacecraft used by NASA for the Artemis lunar exploration program. It consists of a crew module (CM), a space capsule built by Lockheed Martin, and is paired with a European Service Module (ESM) provided by the European Space Agency (ESA) and manufactured by Airbus Defence and Space. Orion supports a crew of four beyond low Earth orbit for up to 21 days undocked or up to six months when docked. It is equipped with a NASA Docking System port and glass cockpit displays. It is intended to be launched atop the Space Launch System (SLS) rocket with a tower-mounted launch escape system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Orion_Snaps_a_Selfie_During_External_Inspection_%28vertical%29.jpg/330px-Orion_Snaps_a_Selfie_During_External_Inspection_%28vertical%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orion_(spacecraft)","wikidata":"Q211727"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Orion_3008_huge.jpg/500px-Orion_3008_huge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Orion_3008_huge.jpg/1280px-Orion_3008_huge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Orion_3008_huge.jpg/500px-Orion_3008_huge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Click on to see large image.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrion_3008_huge.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/OrionCC.jpg/330px-OrionCC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/OrionCC.jpg/330px-OrionCC.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The constellation of Orion, as it can be seen by the naked eye. Lines have been drawn.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AOrionCC.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Sidney_Hall_-_Urania%27s_Mirror_-_Orion_%28best_currently_available_versio